    text: "Round 12 acceptance: npm run release:check with isolated HOME/Git and bun run release:check both PASS all 12 stages at unchanged thresholds. Each passes 169/169 suite tests and 2/2 real packed npm/npx and Bun/bunx consumers, with zero final failures, cancellations or skips. Bun used a disposable public Node 22.23.3 container as UID 1000, with read-only original sources/dependencies and a writable temporary copy. Both report all 20 source files at 100%: 2048/2048 statements and lines, 1304/1304 branches, 107/107 functions. Duplication 0/5199 lines across 46 sources; all 89 declarations documented; production audit zero vulnerabilities; 46 allowed packed files; changelog and publish attestation pass. All 51 authored source/config/test hashes remain unchanged across gates (snapshot fa14595eca072075c0d366852e982310d3dc57e11a759fef2a9eaee51bdfea80). Final affected-file runs: non-root 23/23; root 19 passed plus four explicit permission-bit skips, zero failures; removing only guards gives four expected root failures. Earlier host timing failures and container mount/symlink setup failures were corrected in verification without weakening thresholds or changing package behavior. Strict tracker health without extensions passes 10/10; all 9 items validate. External extension host-version skew and existing development dependency advisories remain outside this review; no new PM CLI defect was identified. Final code changes are limited to four root-only test guards and separating independent assertions. Latest review has no Outside diff range findings. Threads remain untouched; no merge, release, dependency or threshold change."
  - created_at: "2026-10-20T11:16:20.942Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: "Round 13: verified changed-source import updates content while leaving canceled status; byte-identical imports already short-circuit. Plan: mirror remember reopening only in the revision branch; add real non-git tracker lifecycle regressions for all three import harnesses and unchanged archive retention. Self-review: fresh consolidation merges use active snapshots; pending receipts reject canceled targets; package exposes no undo or sync command. Latest CodeRabbit review 5584135803 has no Outside diff range findings. Run behavioral revert proof and both full release gates at unchanged thresholds."
  - created_at: "2026-10-20T11:18:47.737Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: "Round 13 implementation: import revision now mirrors remember by including status=open only for a canceled prior item. Byte-identical branch remains before all update writes. Six non-git lifecycle regressions across claude-code, agents-md and cursor passed; all six failed without the fix with missing active slug after changed re-import. Unchanged phases verify byte-for-byte tracker preservation, archived get/recall/export exclusion, then changed-source recovery. Existing in_progress status survives further revisions. No additional content-writing path requires a fix: remember already reopens, fresh merges select active targets, receipt replay refuses canceled targets, verify/recall/link write operational metadata only; undo and sync are not package commands."
  - created_at: "2026-10-20T11:20:31.258Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: "Round 13 behavioral revert proof: after a green 6/6 run and green pm-linked run, removed only importDir status reopening, kept all tests unchanged, and reran node --test test/review-r13.test.ts: 0 passed, 6 failed with missing active slug at changed-source recovery; restored fix in finally. Extra negative control: injected reopening into the unchanged branch; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"claude-code: unchanged\" test/review-r13.test.ts failed its tracker snapshot equality, proving archive retention assertions detect accidental reopening; restored source in finally. Tracker validation accepts all 9 items; strict health with extensions disabled passes all 10 checks. No tracker history rewritten."
  - created_at: "2026-10-20T11:33:25.022Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: "Round 13 initial full npm release gate: 174/175 tests passed; all 6 new lifecycle cases passed. Sole failure was the existing adversarial base64 email scanner exceeding its unchanged 500ms assertion under shared-host contention. All measured coverage dimensions were 100%, but the full gate correctly failed and removed reports. An independent unchanged scanner repeat completed in 366ms. Retrying the full gate with three-CPU affinity to reduce local test concurrency; no source, dependency, deadline, threshold or test changes."
  - created_at: "2026-10-20T11:56:08.814Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: "Round 13 final acceptance: taskset -c 0,1,2 npm run release:check and taskset -c 0,1,2 bun run release:check both PASS all 12 stages, with isolated HOME/Git settings and unchanged thresholds. Each passes 175/175 suite tests and 2/2 real packed npm/npx and Bun/bunx consumers, with zero final failures, cancellations or skips. Both measure all 20 source files at 100%: 2048/2048 statements and lines, 1310/1310 branches, 107/107 functions. Duplication 0/5261 lines across 47 sources; 89 declarations documented; production audit zero vulnerabilities; 46 allowed packed files; changelog and publish attestation pass. Focused command node --test test/review-r13.test.ts passed 6/6 directly and through pm test; reverting only importDir reopening failed all 6, and the separate unchanged-branch reopening mutation failed snapshot equality. All 55 captured authored source/config/test/doc hashes remain unchanged across both final gates. Initial shared-host timing failure is documented above; no deadlines, thresholds, dependencies or unrelated source changed. Latest review has no Outside diff range findings; no additional content write-path fix was needed. Existing development advisories remain tracked separately; no new PM CLI/SDK defect identified. Claim released for orchestrator verification; item stays in progress. Threads remain untouched; no merge or release."
  - created_at: "2026-10-22T12:02:32.065Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: "PR #6 review verification: reuse the parent context item to track the correction without reopening or re-closing delivered child items. Pulled the remote branch and merged current main, 68a7321c8e11d5f419b7b4653d028b0ccbdbc5df. npm ci passed. Verified unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc6vDHmD: both closure fields on pm-memory-c3gv cite the wrong test file. Current main test/review-r5.test.ts contains the pending merge receipt regression for intervening source/target edits and exactly-once retries; src/consolidate.ts validates source_revision and target_before/target_after. This branch has no implementation difference from main. Correct the two fields through an audited update, append clarification, retain original comments and append-only history, inspect every other PR citation, regenerate the changelog and run tracker-only gates. Latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff findings."
  - created_at: "2026-10-22T12:04:22.730Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: "Evidence proof for the tracker-only correction: both original closure fields cited test/consolidate.test.ts; both now exactly match their prior values except for test/review-r5.test.ts. Verified the named pending merge receipt regression and its source-edit, target-edit, refusal and durable-snapshot assertions directly on current main 68a7321c8e11d5f419b7b4653d028b0ccbdbc5df. Status, closed_at and completed_at remain unchanged (3/3 lifecycle fields), and all 7 changed history streams retain the complete main history as byte-identical prefixes. All implementation, tests and package files match main. Self-review checked every current closure citation in the full PR; the same mistaken citation in the PR description will be corrected, while historical comments and history events are retained with an appended clarification. No other valid instance or outside-diff finding remains. No source-code regression or behavioural revert applies to this evidence-only change."
  - created_at: "2026-10-22T12:06:10.560Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: "PR #6 required tracker-only gates passed: npm ci; npm run changelog:full and npm run changelog:check; strict isolated pm health with required merge drivers (ok=true, exit 0). The linked npm run changelog:check passed 1/1 via pm test pm-memory-0kwy --run --only-last --progress --timeout 600. Evidence verification passed 2/2 corrected closure citations, 3/3 preserved lifecycle fields and 7/7 append-only history prefixes; implementation, test and package files remain identical to current main. No local timeout occurred. No source-code revert is applicable. No new pm CLI/SDK defect established; existing development advisories and the unrelated normal-home extension mismatch remain outside this correction. Keep the parent context item in progress for orchestrator verification and release the claim; no child lifecycle transition, merge, release or review-thread interaction is authorized."
  - created_at: "2026-10-23T15:32:31.658Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: "STALE-CLAIM: audited main 6843a0f3f76d8970d0c08de295aba3759445c029; no open PR or recently pushed live branch references this record. Inspected: src/transfer.ts, test/guidance.test.ts. Remaining: The epic requires lossless import/export, but src/transfer.ts explicitly refuses active validity and consent records because portable harness formats cannot preserve those controls. Complete current portability/parent acceptance and owner verification; do not erase these safeguards or infer full delivery from the base commands. Release historical contention and retain real work as open; no delivery/cancellation is claimed."
